    '**Between the story and Peter’s question.** Peter asks about a count and Jesus answers with a number; the story begins with “Therefore.” The story is not said to answer the count.',
    '**Between the two servants.** One owes ten thousand talents and the other an hundred pence; both fall down and make the same plea; one is released and the other is cast into prison.',
    '**Between the king and the Father.** The story has a king and a lord; Jesus’ application has the heavenly Father. Jesus does not say in so many words that they are the same.',
