A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Lost Sheep and the Lost Coin, the Two Debtors and the Laborers in the Vineyard are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This story makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus answers Peter’s question about forgiving a brother with “Until seventy times seven,” and then compares the kingdom of heaven to a king who takes account of his servants. A servant who owes ten thousand talents is released, and he casts a fellowservant who owes an hundred pence into prison, though the fellowservant pleads in the same words. The lord calls him wicked and delivers him to the tormentors, and Jesus says that his heavenly Father will do so likewise to those who do not forgive their brother from their hearts.'))
