A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names a certain king, the heavenly Father who does so likewise, the hearers addressed as “you,” and a brother whose trespasses are forgiven or not, and nothing more. No identity for the king, the servant, the fellowservant, the debts, the prison or the tormentors. No symbol carried in from another parable. Forgiving, refusing and paying are actions in a story, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is neither the servant nor the fellowservant. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))

